cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: "Please cite this software when using LLM-CA, and record the version or commit used."
title: "LLM-CA Simulation and Benchmark Platform"
authors:
  - name: "LLM-CA contributors"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kmichalakis/LLM-CA"
abstract: >-
  A Python framework for context-reasoning simulations across pervasive
  environments. It provides synthetic scenarios, interchangeable reasoners,
  evidence and action evaluation, annotation workflows, a GUI, and reports.
  Synthetic offline results do not establish real-world effectiveness or
  controlled large-language-model performance.
keywords:
  - context awareness
  - pervasive computing
  - simulation
  - reproducibility
  - large language models
